.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1037 AM PDT Thu Sep 10 2026

Currently VFR with high clouds. Moderate confidence on ceilings on
the cusp of IFR/MVFR returning to bayshore and coastal terminals
tonight. Satellite shows a surprisingly decent push of stratus just
beginning to enter our coastal waters from the north. Reasonable
worst case scenario is a more compressed marine layer will bring
lower ceilings and visibilities (likely LIFR); however, that would
likely remain confined to the immediate coast. Diurnal winds will
prevail.

Vicinity of SFO...Currently VFR with northwesterly flow. Moderate
confidence on a ceiling on the cusp of IFR/MVFR developing tonight.
Diurnal winds will prevail.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Currently VFR with northwesterly flow at
both terminals. Moderate confidence on IFR ceilings returning
tonight. Diurnal winds will prevail.

